QuestGuidance.Register("en",252,{
[8033]="70043A9F\n1\tTalk to Istien\tTalk to Istien to complete Volume IV, Book 3!\n",
[8034]="7004560B\n1\tTalk to Istien\tTalk to Istien to complete Volume IV, Book 4!\n",
[8035]="70048787\n1\tTalk to Istien\tTalk to Istien to complete Volume IV, Book 7!\n",
[8036]="7004B310\n1\tTalk to Istien\tTalk to Istien to complete Volume IV, Book 8!\n",
[8037]="70046395\n1\tTalk to Istien\tTalk to Istien to complete Volume IV, Books 5 and 6!\n",
[8038]="70043DFB\n1\tDestroy enemy barricades (total: 10)\tEnemy barricades can be found on the Western side of Osgiliath. Destroy the enemy barricades.\n2\tSpeak with Shíktarb\tShíktarb is at Shrak Mauruk. You should listen to Shíktarb yell at you.\n",
[8039]="70059871\n1\tDefeat Lhudblath the Silver Warg\tLhudblath the Silver Warg can be found in the eastern Wildwood. Linnet has asked you to defeat the Silver Warg, Lhudblath.\n2\tTalk to Linnet\tLinnet is located in the south-central Wildwood. You should talk to Linnet Redholm.\n",
[8040]="70039758\n1\tTalk to Calin\tYou should speak with Calin when you are ready to go to the Mead Hall.\n2\tSpeak with Herubrand\tSpeak with Herubrand in the basement of the farm-house in Woodhurst.\n",
[8041]="700588F9\n1\tDwarf-captives can be found in the Angmarim town of Dûn Traikh, in western Elderslade. You should free dwarf-captives before they are forced to make weapons for the enemy.\t\n2\tReturn to Zádokh Flint-eye\tZádokh Flint-eye can be found at Drenghól. You have freed the dwarves in Dûn Traikh. Return to Zádokh Flint-eye for your reward.\n",
[8042]="70032BE1\n1\tFind a leader among the infected Orcs\030Find a leader among the infected spiders\tThe leader of the infected Orcs should be among his minions to the south-east of Knakk's camp, as well as the Queen lurking among her brood to the east.\n2\tReturn to Knakk\tKnakk is camped on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of Redhorn Lodes.\n",
[8043]="7005465E\n1\tDefeat Draulush the Bloody\030Defeat Mangath the Impervious\030Defeat Narnagír the White-arrow\tLegolas has identified the leaders of the Bloodless in Kaslokroz. You should defeat Draulush, Mangath, and Narnagír.\n",
[8044]="7000874E\n1\tReturn to Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag\030Collect Lieutenants' seals (total: 3)\tPositions held by the enemy are often watched over by the lieutenants in their army. You may even find a lieutenant flanked by sergeants in the wild-lands. Chieftain Durulkum commanded that you retrieve the seals worn by the lieutenants in the enemy army and return them to him at Dâr-gazag.\n",
[8045]="7001CCD7\n1\tCollect ninglyr (total: 10)\tNinglyr may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angened. Gaerfalas has asked you to gather ninglor flowers for use in preparing medicines.\n2\tBring ninglyr to Gaerfalas atop Amon Angened\tGaerfalas is at the way-post atop Amon Angened, east of Fállug. You should bring the flowers you collected to Gaerfalas.\n",
[8046]="7004D073\n1\tFind a stray animal\030Find some old clothes\030Find a broken toy\030Make suspicious Dale-folk leave (total: 6)\tYou should gather items for the Easterling refugees so that they can assist the city of Dale.\n2\tDorwinion and Chayasír can be found in and around the city of Dale. You should bring them the items they requested.\t\n3\tTalk to Erna\tYou should return to the Queen Regent Erna, who can be found in the Great-keep in Dale.\n",
[8047]="70066672\n1\tFishing nets can be found along the River Morthond near Sardol in the Blackroot Vale. Gordir has asked you to search for fish in the nearby fishing nets and bring any fish you find to him. You should search the nets.\t\n2\tDeliver the fish to Gordir in Sardol\tGordir can be found along the River Morthond in Sardol. You have searched the nets as Gordir asked and found a few fish caught in them. You should deliver the fish to Gordir.\n3\tFish with Gordir along the River Morthond (total: 3)\tGordir can be found on a pier along the River Morthond in Sardol. You have delivered the fish caught in the nets to Gordir, and he has asked you to fish with him for a time. You should fish with Gordir.\n4\tTalk to Gordir\tGordir can be found along the River Morthond in Sardol. You have fished with Gordir and caught three pike out of the River Morthond. You should talk to Gordir.\n",
[8048]="70017534\n1\tAssist Lar in ridding Skûmfil of gredbyg\030Assist Moggi in ridding Skûmfil of gredbyg\030Collect samples from the gredbyg of Skûmfil for Pentlenn\tLar, Moggi, and Pentlenn are at the Shadowed Refuge. Mallas has told you that he will speak well for you to Veúlfur at the Twenty-first Hall after you have assisted his agents in the Shadowed Refuge.\n2\tTalk to Mallas at the Shadowed Refuge\tMallas is at the Shadowed Refuge. You have completed all the tasks set before you by Lar, Moggi, and Pentlenn. You should now return to Mallas and inform him that your efforts are complete.\n",
[8049]="7004744F\n1\tCollect horsetail seeds (total: 6)\030Collect vetchling seeds (total: 6)\030Collect oxlip seeds (total: 6)\tSeeds of oxlip, horsetail, and vetchling can be found on the Field of Cormallen to the west of Henneth Annûn. Ereblen has asked you to gather more seeds from the Field of Cormallen and return to him with as many as you are able to bear.\n2\tDeliver the seeds to Ereblen in Henneth Annûn\tEreblen can be found in Henneth Annûn. You have gathered many seeds and should now deliver them to Ereblen.\n",
[8050]="70035598\n1\tUncover frozen plants in the Balewood (total: 8)\tSnowdrifts can be found throughout south-west Balewood. Mossbeard wants you to uncover plants that might be freezing beneath snowdrifts in the Balewood and expose them to whatever light remains in the darkened forest.\n2\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard can be found at your side or if you have become separated, you can use your whistle to call him. You have uncovered many plants that were freezing beneath snowdrifts in south-west Balewood. You should now talk to Mossbeard and see what more can be done.\n",
[8051]="7004DA3A\n1\tCollect saplings (total: 6)\tSaplings can be found just south of Felegoth. You should gather saplings that are to be planted around the forest.\n2\tClear dead trees (total: 10)\030Plant saplings in fertile soil (quantity: see journal)\tFertile soil and dead trees can both be found throughout Eryn Lasgalen. You should clear away the dead trees and plant the saplings in fertile soil around the forest.\n3\tTalk to Radagast\tYou should return to Radagast, who can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth.\n",
[8052]="70071624\n1\tComplete 'Session: Life on the Other Side'\tMizâdi has agreed to hear Kotráka Saiya's story. You should talk to Kotráka Saiya and complete the Session.\n2\tTalk to Kotráka Saiya\tYou have heard Kotráka Saiya's story. You should talk to Kotráka Saiya.\n3\tTalk to Mizâdi\tYou have heard Kotráka Saiya's story. You should talk to Mizâdi to hear what she thinks.\n",
[8053]="70068B6A\n1\tTalk to Jidâlo outside the Broken Pillar Tavern in the Lower Ward\tShajât's former captain, Jidâlo, is outside the Broken Pillar Tavern in the Lower Ward.\n2\tTalk to the Ballast's former ship-mates (total: 6)\tThe Ballast's former ship-mates can be found in the vicinity of the Broken Pillar Tavern, in the Lower Ward.\n3\tBring the coins raised by his ship-mates to Shajât outside the Lower Ward\tShajât is outside the Lower Ward, in the Sail-haven.\n4\tFind the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower Ward\tExcited to begin his new life, Shajât agreed to meet you outside the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.\n5\tTalk to Shajât outside the Swain's Guild Hall\tShajât stands outside the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.\n6\tRetrieve Shajât's coins from ruffians in the Gut (total: 6)\tShajât lost the coins given to him by his ship-mates to ruffians in the Gut, and if you don't recover them for him no one will.\n7\tReturn his coins to Shajât outside the Swain's Guild Hall\tShajât stands outside the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.\n",
[8054]="700001AB\n1\tFree slaves in Carn Dûm (total: 2)\tCarn Dûm lies to the west of Tármunn Súrsa. Éa's husband Erscin and his fellow warriors were captured by Orcs and taken to Carn Dûm. She has asked you to enter Carn Dûm and rescue Erscin.\n2\tTalk to Éa\tÉa is at Tármunn Súrsa, east of Carn Dûm. The slaves of Carn Dûm were set free and may now return to their homes, but you were unable to find Éa's husband, Erscin. You should return to Éa with the news.\n",
[8055]="70052CE4\n1\tDefeat wandering lost-lights (total: 8)\tWandering lost-lights can be found along the river Gladden. You should defeat wandering lost-lights.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many wandering lost-lights.\n",
[8056]="70017599\n1\tUse the tome to summon Ruingal\030Defeat Ruingal\tEnter the Forges of Khazad-dûm, summon the fire grim, Ruingal, and slay it.\n2\tTalk to Winiel at the Rotting Cellar\tWiniel is at the Rotting Cellar in the Water Works, north-east from the Forges of Khazad-dûm. You should return to Winiel with tidings of your victory.\n",
[8057]="70025A77\n1\tDefeat the creature beneath the lighthouse\tThe ruins of the lighthouse are south-east of the colossus. Gaelnarthan asked you to venture into the lighthouse and defeat the creature you find within.\n2\tTalk to Gaelnarthan at the colossus camp\tGaelnarthan is at the colossus camp. Gaelnarthan will be pleased to hear the kergrim hunting them has been defeated.\n",
[8058]="7002E4FA\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Edgal\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
